  "behavior": [
    "Exact owned legacy company/unsigned pair lookup reads at most two rows, rejects ambiguity and validates exact original coordinates. It preserves missing/unbound/bound distinctions without scanning pages.",
    "Pure preparation verifies the group pair against both original canonical users and the original binding creator, retaining original company/conversation/room coordinates.",
    "Original state assessment requires already complete encryption/membership/settings. Missing state cannot authorize repair, replacement or adoption.",
    "Actual Synapse lets the canonical peer join the exact original room using its retained original user/device after a group login. Original creator and both signed keys survive restart, with no impersonation, new group alias, provider logout or key replacement."
  ],
  "validation": [
    "All 99 domain cases pass, including three new original-room cases.",
    "Eight actual PostgreSQL repository cases pass, including exact pair lookup, foreign ownership, malformed/ambiguous readback, cancellation/interruption and original parent purge.",
    "All three actual Synapse room cases pass: prior cross-company new room and lost response cases plus the original-peer join/key retention/restart case.",
    "Format and architecture checks pass; 8,374 sources remain unchanged during the 144.409-second gate."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "No migration, constructor/DI, endpoint, worker or Mobile product caller changed. No fresh API/worker result is represented.",
    "Provider control and public-key continuity do not prove SDK encrypted message transport or native group room authority.",
    "Durable request/publication lifecycle, current admission and legacy-producer creation fences remain required before rollout.",
    "Live schema116, phone28 and group-disabled status remain unchanged; all54 PRD groups stay open."
  ],
  "continuation": "Implement group-owned room preparation/publication with current native/device/peer admission around bounded provider work, immutable binding, stable alias recovery and explicit original-unbound handling; then recipient keys/content/sync/push and full Mobile adoption."
